# Intent: Review fix (2026-11-16). The remote token gate (TC01) passed every call whose source was not "remote", and the caller chooses that field, so one host bug that left it out let a controller act with no cue. Now the unit has a second floor that does not read source: while a remote session is on, a cued kind (a head move beyond 45 degrees yaw or 45 degrees pitch, find, photo, dance, game, listen) from any call that is not marked remote must carry the session's own host id as its token (the paired host announces it in self.remote.session as the new host property and stamps it on every call that is not a controller's), or a valid cue token for that kind. Anything else is ignored, logged as not_host in self.remote.history and answered {"ok":false,"reason":"not_host"}. With no session on, with an older host that announced no id, and for a head move inside the safe range, nothing changes. The id is dropped with the session, so a stale id never opens a new one.
# Placement: unit (the robot refuses a cued action it was not shown to the person for); the host half is host/maipai_body/remote_trust.py
# Upstream: main/hal/{maipai_remote_core.h,maipai_remote.cc,maipai_remote.h,hal_mcp.cpp} (ours, patches TB05, TC01 and TC04)
# Check after a flash: host/tests/firmware/remote_floor_test.c passes on the PC; with the host running and a controller session open, self.robot.dance with no token answers not_host and the same call from the host's own page plays; self.robot.set_head_angles yaw 20 with no token still moves.

